  "prompt": "You are a renowned cognitive scientist analyzing computational models of the two-step decision task (Daw et al.). Below is a Python cognitive model that was fit to participant 6's behavior.\n\n```python\ndef cognitive_model2(action_1, state, action_2, reward, model_parameters):\n    \"\"\"\n    Hybrid Model with Single Temperature and Reward-Modulated Stickiness for Both Stages.\n    Uses a single beta parameter to allow for win-stay/lose-shift parameters at both stages without exceeding 8 parameters.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    alpha: [0, 1] - Learning rate.\n    beta: [0, 10] - Shared inverse temperature for both stages.\n    w: [0, 1] - Model-based weight.\n    p_1_win: [-5, 5] - Stage 1 stickiness after a rewarded trial.\n    p_1_lose: [-5, 5] - Stage 1 stickiness after an unrewarded trial.\n    p_2_win: [-5, 5] - Stage 2 stickiness after a rewarded trial.\n    p_2_lose: [-5, 5] - Stage 2 stickiness after an unrewarded trial.\n    lam: [0, 1] - Eligibility trace.\n    \"\"\"\n    alpha, beta, w, p_1_win, p_1_lose, p_2_win, p_2_lose, lam = model_parameters\n    n_trials = len(action_1)\n  \n    transition_matrix = np.array([[0.7, 0.3], [0.3, 0.7]])\n    p_choice_1 = np.zeros(n_trials)\n    p_choice_2 = np.zeros(n_trials)\n    q_stage1_mf = np.zeros(2)\n    q_stage2_mf = np.zeros((2, 2))\n    \n    last_action_1 = -1\n    last_action_2 = -1\n    last_reward = -1\n\n    for trial in range(n_trials):\n        a1 = int(action_1[trial])\n        s = int(state[trial])\n        a2 = int(action_2[trial])\n        r = reward[trial]\n\n        max_q_stage2 = np.max(q_stage2_mf, axis=1)\n        q_stage1_mb = transition_matrix @ max_q_stage2\n        q_stage1_net = w * q_stage1_mb + (1 - w) * q_stage1_mf\n        \n        stickiness_1 = np.zeros(2)\n        if last_action_1 != -1:\n            if last_reward == 1:\n                stickiness_1[last_action_1] = p_1_win\n            elif last_reward == 0:\n                stickiness_1[last_action_1] = p_1_lose\n            \n        logits_1 = beta * q_stage1_net + stickiness_1\n        logits_1 -= np.max(logits_1)\n        exp_q1 = np.exp(logits_1)\n        probs_1 = exp_q1 / np.sum(exp_q1)\n        p_choice_1[trial] = probs_1[a1]\n\n        stickiness_2 = np.zeros(2)\n        if last_action_2 != -1:\n            if last_reward == 1:\n                stickiness_2[last_action_2] = p_2_win\n            elif last_reward == 0:\n                stickiness_2[last_action_2] = p_2_lose\n            \n        logits_2 = beta * q_stage2_mf[s] + stickiness_2\n        logits_2 -= np.max(logits_2)\n        exp_q2 = np.exp(logits_2)\n        probs_2 = exp_q2 / np.sum(exp_q2)\n        p_choice_2[trial] = probs_2[a2]\n\n        delta_stage1 = q_stage2_mf[s, a2] - q_stage1_mf[a1]\n        q_stage1_mf[a1] += alpha * delta_stage1\n        \n        delta_stage2 = r - q_stage2_mf[s, a2]\n        q_stage2_mf[s, a2] += alpha * delta_stage2\n        \n        q_stage1_mf[a1] += alpha * lam * delta_stage2\n        \n        last_action_1 = a1\n        last_action_2 = a2\n        last_reward = r\n\n    eps = 1e-10\n    log_loss = -(np.sum(np.log(p_choice_1 + eps)) + np.sum(np.log(p_choice_2 + eps)))\n    return log_loss\n```\n\nList every distinct psychological mechanism in this model. A mechanism is one separable computational assumption (e.g. \"MB/MF mixture weight\", \"choice stickiness\", \"reward-dependent stickiness\", \"separate stage-2 learning rate\", \"value decay/forgetting\", \"eligibility trace\", \"optimistic Q initialization\").\n\nReturn STRICT JSON only (no prose, no markdown fences):\n{\"mechanisms\": [{\"name\": \"short snake_case id\", \"title\": \"human name\", \"description\": \"one sentence\", \"params\": [{\"name\": \"param name as in code\", \"bounds\": [lo, hi]}], \"evidence\": \"the exact code lines implementing it\", \"expressible_in_slots\": true, \"reason\": \"only when expressible_in_slots is false: why the slot contract cannot express this mechanism faithfully\"}]}